1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,060
Listen to a talk on an archaeology podcast.

2
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:12,230
Man: Throughout the years, archaeologists have discovered many fascinating artifacts on the Greek island of Crete.

3
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:15,448
One example is the Phaistos disc,

4
00:00:15,448 --> 00:00:24,030
an ancient clay artifact that was found in the ruins of the Minoan palace at Phaistos.

5
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:31,276
The Minoan civilization lasted from about 3100 BCE to 1100 BCE,

6
00:00:31,276 --> 00:00:39,180
and we think this artifact was made in the second millennium BCE.

7
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:44,436
It was discovered in 1908 and it features many stamped symbols,

8
00:00:44,456 --> 00:00:49,210
241 to be exact, in the shape of a spiral

9
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:56,000
The symbols, they include images of things like animals, tools, and so on.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,050
These animals, tools, and other images form a pattern in the shape of a spiral.

11
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:11,110
What's so interesting is that these symbols are unlike anything else from the Minoan civilization or any other known writing system.

12
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:15,210
Many experts have tried to decipher these enigmatic symbols.

13
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:19,260
Some suggest they could represent an unknown language.

14
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:24,640
Others think they might represent a calendar or even a religious hymn

15
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:28,180
yet no consensus has been reached.

16
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:35,210
Another intriguing thing about the Phaistos disc is the method used to imprint the symbols.

17
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:41,170
This involved pressing prefabricated stamps into wet clay.

18
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,070
This process is really remarkable.

19
00:01:44,070 --> 00:01:49,110
It suggests a level of sophistication similar to early printing.

20
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:55,316
Some scholars hypothesize that the disc might be an import from another culture,

21
00:01:55,316 --> 00:02:00,090
a lone artifact brought to Crete by traders or travelers.

22
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:08,130
But this is another point of contention surrounding this fascinating artifact.
